Поскольку 
\begin_inset Formula $b=\mathrm{const}$
\end_inset

,
 могу проинтегрировать 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
w'=-\rho\frac{2bk\dot{\theta}^{2}}{r^{2}}+\frac{2bgk\tan\alpha}{r^{2}}
\]

\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula 
\[
w=-\frac{\rho^{2}}{2}\frac{2bk\dot{\theta}^{2}}{r^{2}}+\frac{2bgk\tan\alpha}{r^{2}}\rho+C_{1}
\]

\end_inset

выражаю 
\begin_inset Formula $f$
\end_inset

:
 
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
f=\frac{2b\left(k-1\right)\tan\alpha}{\left(k+1\right)}+\frac{2c\tan\alpha}{\left(k+1\right)}=\mathrm{const}
\]

\end_inset

далее 
